# GENIE.AI fork of OPEA v1.5 comps/dataprep/src/requirements.in.
# Source: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/opea-project/GenAIComps/v1.5/comps/dataprep/src/requirements.in
# Regenerate the lock with:
#   uv pip compile --generate-hashes --python-version 3.11 --python-platform x86_64-manylinux_2_31 requirements.in -o requirements-cpu.txt
#
# Deltas vs upstream (compiled-lock source, PRD FR-4):
#   - opencv-python -> opencv-python-headless (server image has no display; the
#     two packages conflict — both provide cv2 — so headless is the direct dep).
#     NOTE: the compiled lock still contains BOTH (opencv-python pulled
#     transitively via unstructured-inference; headless listed directly). The
#     dual cv2 install is a 2.5 dataprep re-audit item; the headless pin keeps
#     the direct dependency correct for the display-less server image.
#   - psycopg2 -> psycopg2-binary (avoid source compile).
#   - openai-whisper kept (v1.5 pins it; verify it builds — arch decision D8).
#   - docling/docling-core/langchain/fastapi/docarray pinned to the versions
#     OPEA v1.5's compiled lock ships — recompiling the bare .in today resolves
#     to newer packages (e.g. docling 2.119) that do NOT pair with v1.5 comps
#     source. These pins reproduce the v1.5 known-good set (AC1 requires
#     docling-core==2.44.2).
#   - overlay extras + opentelemetry instrumentation appended below.

